Gragas, Vi, Fizz, Galio, Kayn, Orn, Poppy, Rakan, Pyke, Rell, Riven, Tryndamere, Urgot, Yone, Zac, Renekton, Nidalee, Fiora, Camille, BelVeth

Core travel-window dashes where Flash can be buffered in the wind-up / travel window to angle-correct / extend the end point of the dash itself and make the intrinsic damage / hard CC on arrival of that dash land more reliably and more optimally.

Stable high confidence set:
Gragas E Barrel Roll, Vi Q Vault Breaker, Fizz E Playful / Trickster, Kayn Q Darkest Slash / Umbral Dash, Poppy E Heroic Charge, Pyke E Bone Skewer, Rell W Ferromancy: Charge, Riven Q3 Shockwave, Tryndamere E Spinning Slash, Yone Q3, Zac E Elastic Slingshot, Renekton E Slice and Dice, Nidalee W Pounce, Fiora Q Lunge, Camille E Hookshot.

Majority now converging additions:
Orn E Tectonic Break – lunge with knock-up on arrival whose hitbox follows the travel and can be angle-corrected by a flash buffer;
Galio E Winds of War – linear dash with damage / CC on arrival, flash buffer extends / angle corrects the arrival;
BelVeth Q – in-flight dash with intrinsic damage on arrival that is angle-corrected by a flash buffer.

Disputed but consistent with the improve-the-dash-its-own-landing criterion:
Rakan W Gleam – dash to target with damage and knock-up on arrival, flash buffer is used to make the intrinsic CC / damage of the dash itself land;
Urgot E Slide – sliding dash with damage / slow on arrival, flash buffer can be used to improve the landing of the slide’s own damage / CC.

Excluded under the “improve the dash’s own damage / CC landing, not repositioning only or follow-up enable” definition:
LeBlanc W Distortion – instant blink / reposition-follow-up;
Shen E Shadow Dash – teleport-to-ally reposition;
Tristana W Rocket Jump – pure mobility / escape reposition;
Corki W Valkyrie – mobility reposition;
Sejuani Q Permafrost – skillshot slow, not a dash;
Jarvan E+Q – flash use is primarily to enable the follow-up Q / Cataclysm rather than to improve the E’s own Dragon Strike CC / damage landing.

This narrows the set to the classic travel dashes plus Orn, Galio and BelVeth, with Rakan W and Urgot E kept as the remaining plausible dash-landing optimizations and Jarvan E+Q kept out as a follow-up enable tech.

